1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,000
IncuBrix creator lead engine: one command, python -m engine run. Python standard library only, no API keys, $0.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:23,500
28 offline tests run in about a second, including a regression test for every audit error found while checking my own leads.

3
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Normal run on a brand-new input: real, recently active podcasts the engine has never seen. It finds, verifies, dedupes, scores, picks a channel and drafts messages.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Run history: the full-scale run covered 20,000+ shows, gave 1,048 qualified creators and 0 duplicates, in minutes, at $0 cost.

5
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:13,000
One qualified lead: every claim (country, activity, sponsor or offer, need, contact) has a public evidence URL an auditor can open.

6
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Refresh on another new input: new creators get new lead IDs, existing creators keep theirs, and the country cap re-balances automatically.

7
00:01:41,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Failure test: a simulated crash after 5 feeds. Progress is saved, and the error is logged to output/errors.csv.

8
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Recovery: the same command again reuses the 5 saved feeds and fetches only the rest. Nothing is duplicated.

9
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Priority A outreach: a personalised first message about the creator's latest episode, 2 follow-ups and a backup-channel touch, each with sender identity, opt-out and a tracked link.

10
00:02:47,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Launch kit: the step-by-step week-1 plan IncuBrix can start on Monday, with owners, tools and daily volumes.
